Adding env to docker

1. Create a .env File
2. docker build -t fostersoasare/mafoil
3. Pass the environment when running the image
  docker run --env-file .env -p 8000:8000 fostersoasare/mafoil


Login to docker 
When you use google to login to docker , you will need to generate tokens and use it as password
- Account Settings
- In the Security section, select Personal access tokens.
- Generate new token.
- Add a description for your token
- Set the access permissions
- Generate 

docker login
Enter username 
Paste password : NB: The keystrokes don't show when you paste password

WSL Error on Windows 11
Run cmd as an admin
- wsl --uninstall
- wsl --install
- wsl --install -d Ubuntu



net start com.docker.service

The error code 0x800701bc indicates that your Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL) needs a kernel update in order to use WSL 2
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install-manual#step-4---download-the-linux-kernel-update-package
or wsl.exe --update
https://docs.docker.com/desktop/install/windows-install/

Turn Windows features on or off
Windows Hypervisor Platform
Virtual Machine Platform
Windows Subsystem For Linx (WSL)
Uncheck and restart 
Then check and restart
wsl --status
wsl --update
wsl --set-default-version 2

Enable Virtual Machine Platform:
dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:VirtualMachinePlatform /all /norestart

DISM /Online /Enable-Feature /All /FeatureName:Microsoft-Hyper-V
bcdedit /set hypervisorlaunchtype auto

Enable WSL Feature (if not already enabled):
dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux /all /norestart

CMD npm run start

STOPPING A CONTAINER
docker ps
docker kill CONTAINERID

docker images
docker rmi imageId imageID imageID